  "title": "75 lb of cocaine kills a 175‑lb bear in Georgia woods",
  "description": "In 1985 a plane dumped a massive cocaine shipment over the Tennessee wilderness. A black bear ate the powder, overdosed, and later became a taxidermied attraction that even officiates weddings.\n\nThe story shows how a criminal mistake created a bizarre piece of Americana that still draws visitors today.\n\nBased on the Wikipedia article \"Cocaine Bear (bear)\" (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cocaine_Bear_(bear)), licensed CC BY-SA 4.0.\n\nImages from Wikimedia Commons:\nCocaine Bear, Kentucky for Kentucky Fun Mall (cropped).jpg (Ferrett333, CC BY-SA 4.0): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cocaine_Bear,_Kentucky_for_Kentucky_Fun_Mall_(cropped).jpg\nCocaine Bear, Kentucky for Kentucky Fun Mall.jpg (Ferrett333, CC BY-SA 4.0): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cocaine_Bear,_Kentucky_for_Kentucky_Fun_Mall.jpg\n\n3D models:\nMSCC007 Ursus americanus Left Mandible by The Mammoth Site of Hot Springs, SD, Inc. (CC BY 4.0) https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/none-5fd23637ab3b48e2aad88e2e7e53af7f\nPlastic container by jesperlindstrom93 (CC BY 4.0) https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/none-c846c3fd2686446d82985869f62fd258",
